# Codex Task — Add Mineflayer Smoke-Test Runner

WTrader already contains `MineflayerGameClientAdapter`, but there is currently no executable CLI/runtime entry point for it.

Do not redesign the adapter.

Create:

```text
apps/minecraft-executor/src/mineflayer-main.ts
```

and add package script:

```json
"mineflayer": "tsx apps/minecraft-executor/src/mineflayer-main.ts"
```

The runner must instantiate the existing `MineflayerGameClientAdapter`.

Read configuration from environment variables:

```text
MINECRAFT_HOST
MINECRAFT_PORT
MINECRAFT_USERNAME
MINECRAFT_VERSION
MINECRAFT_PROFILES_FOLDER
```

Defaults:

```text
MINECRAFT_PORT=25565
MINECRAFT_PROFILES_FOLDER=.minecraft-auth
```

Do not hardcode credentials.

## Runtime behavior

On start:

1. print sanitized connection configuration;
2. subscribe to all normalized `GameClientEvent`s;
3. connect;
4. wait for READY;
5. print connection/kick/error diagnostics;
6. remain running until SIGINT/SIGTERM.

Do not automatically buy or sell anything.

## Interactive stdin commands

Support a minimal local debug console:

```text
/ah
/cmd <minecraft command>
/gui
/inventory
/state
/quit
```

`/ah` must call the existing:

```ts
adapter.openAuctionHouse()
```

`/cmd` must call:

```ts
adapter.executeCommand()
```

`/gui` prints the current normalized GUI snapshot in a readable form:

```text
title
id
slotCount

for each non-empty slot:
slot
itemType
displayName
quantity
lore
```

`/inventory` prints normalized inventory.

`/state` prints adapter state.

## Event logging

For GUI events print concise structured output:

```text
[GUI_OPENED]
title=Auction (Page 1)
id=...
slots=...

slot=...
item=minecraft:anvil
name=...
lore=...
```

For `GUI_UPDATED`, print changed information without flooding the terminal.

For kicks/errors, print the exact raw reason.

## Important

Keep this runner observation/debug oriented.

Do not add anti-bot bypass, fingerprint spoofing, CAPTCHA bypass, ban evasion, or protection-evasion logic.

Do not add autonomous purchasing yet.

## Validation

Add tests where practical.

Then run:

```text
pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
pnpm build
pnpm test
```

At the end print the exact command the owner should use to start the Mineflayer runtime.
